From: Jack Rao <jack.rao@baseten.co>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 22:44:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] perf(dsa): env-gated packed-CP layout cache
 (BT_DSA_CP_LAYOUT_CACHE) [baseten]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Under packed THD + allgather CP, every layer's forward rebuilds the
packed CP layout (query positions + gathered-KV reorder) via
dsa_layout.build_packed_allgather_cp_query_positions_and_key_reorder —
17x5 boolean-mask indexes (each an aten::nonzero + D2H sync) per
layer-microbatch, i.e. 26,520 host syncs and ~150k kernel launches per
78-layer 2-microbatch step including the full-recompute replay. The
result is a pure function of the microbatch's (cu_seqlens_q,
cu_seqlens_kv, cp_size, cp_rank, sizes) — identical across layers and
across the recompute replay.

Cache the builder results on the packed_seq_params carrier — the same
per-microbatch lifetime pattern as the existing
_dsa_index_share_topk_holder. Entries key on the full argument tuple and
hit only on object identity of the input cu_seqlens tensors (refs held
in the entry), so stale reads are impossible; cached tensors are the
identical objects from the first computation, so reuse is bitwise exact.
Downstream consumers are read-only (index_select / mask construction).
All three call sites covered (main cp_size>1 branch, the
sequence-parallel-TP branch, _build_kv_reorder_idx).

Env-gated, default OFF; gate off => byte-identical path. One-time
WARNING gate-state line per process, so a present-but-inert patch is
never silent (the Aug-9 v1 lesson on the sibling FIX A gate).

Evidence (LPS-1062, 2026-08-09, GLM-5.2-FP8 LoRA, golden EP16/CP16,
131k x 4 microbatches, 2x8 B300): together with the companion
BT_THD_ROPE_HOST_CACHE, 634-645 -> ~715 tok/s/GPU steady (+11-13%);
16k x d32 customer shape 612 -> 726 (+18.5%). Loss canary drift <=2e-3,
memory flat, baseline triple-replicated. Mechanism: launch-pipeline
decompression (GPU-union idle 8.52s -> 1.82s per step), not comm
de-staggering (SendRecv totals flat).
Parity: test_dsa_cp_layout_cache_parity.py — 191 PASS (CPU), cached vs
direct bitwise across cp sizes/ranks/docs/padding, miss/hit/identity
safety, under the production checkpoint-replay context.
Records: experiment_artefacts/glm/lps_1062_perf/runs/
overnight_20260809_dispatcher_hostsync/ (REPORT.md, PATCH_NOTES.md,
ATTRIBUTION.md).

PP2/CP8/EP8 @131k A/B on the 73c24b00 lineage (2026-08-13, LPS-1062
E2 spec section 3b): <TO FILL TONIGHT — d4 vs 918, d16 vs 1052
tok/s/GPU; canary band loss 12.2-12.4, grad-norm comparable>
